 "notes": "B-L gauged dark-photon DM (main result of the paper). Curve = lower envelope of the three solid x/y/z-axis limits (red/green/orange, cos theta=1) in Fig.3, derived from real LISA Pathfinder April-2016 auxiliary-channel (SC-vs-TM relative acceleration) data. Fig.3 y-axis is the relative coupling eps_{B-L}; the gauge coupling is g_{B-L}=eps_{B-L}*e (Eq.1). Per the compilation convention for LPF B-L, eps is reported DIRECTLY as g_BL WITHOUT the *e (=0.303) factor (the *e factor is removed in the reference file); the same eps values appear as g_{B-L}=eps*e in Fig.5. Blue dashed/dot-dashed/dotted curves are forecasts (projections), not reported. Limit from SNR<=1 estimate (no explicit statistical CL stated; 0.95 assumed). rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm3 assumed (density-dependent). World-leading over 4e-19<m<3e-17 eV; full curve extends to ~4e-15 eV. Vector-extracted from figure_3.pdf, tick-calibrated.",
